# Build artifacts
/target/
**/target/
# Any alternate cargo build dir, whatever it is called. Two cargo invocations
# must never share one CARGO_TARGET_DIR — they take the same lock, so a
# foreground build silently blocks behind a background test suite — so a lane
# running a long workspace test in the background needs a second dir for its
# interactive edit-build-test cycle, and a third for a probe build that must
# not disturb either. This line replaces four separate patterns
# (`target-test/`, `target-hl/`, `target-hl[0-9]*/`, and a `target-probe/` that
# had to be added when the fourth one appeared). Neither the count nor the
# names are principled — they are however many concurrent cargo invocations a
# lane happens to have, named for whatever they were doing — so match the
# shape instead of enumerating the instances. The contents are the same either
# way: codegen units and rlibs we never want to commit.
**/target-*/
**/*.rs.bk
# Stray rustc codegen-unit objects written to the Windows `nul` device name
# (these land in the crate root, not target/, when a build/clippy invocation
# redirects output to `nul` on Windows).
**/nul.*.rcgu.o

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS images
*.iso
*.img
*.hdd
*.ext4
# Written beside rootfs.ext4 by scripts/ctest-fixtures.py image-stamp: the
# sha256 of every locally built ELF packed into it. It describes a gitignored
# artifact, so tracking it would assert something about an image that does not
# exist in a fresh clone.
*.ext4.manifest

# Limine binary artifacts (downloaded at build time)
/limine/

# Reference upstream clones (study material; embedded git repos, never tracked)
/dolphin/
/kglobalaccel/
/nushell/
/plasma-desktop/
/plasma-workspace/

# Toolchain sysroot — populated by cargo build of `posix` and
# `toolchain/stubs` (libc.a, libstubs.a, libunwind.a). Pure build
# output that must be regenerated per-machine; never commit.
#
# This deliberately covers `.sysroot.stamp` too, and that is not an oversight
# to be "fixed" by tracking it. Unlike the ctest fixture stamps — which sit
# beside tracked ELFs and must survive a fresh clone — the sysroot stamp
# describes *this machine's* libc.a. A tracked copy would arrive in a checkout
# asserting that a libc.a you have not built yet was built from those sources,
# which is the precise false-green the stamp exists to prevent. Absent stamp =
# "nobody has built the sysroot here", which is the truth on a fresh clone, and
# the checker falls back to mtime and says so.
/toolchain/sysroot/

# Orchestrator history (personal)
.orchestrator_history

# Saved web pages (reference material, not code)
*.html
*_files/

# OS-specific
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Local safety backup taken before the 2026-06-13 todo.txt issue migration
todo.backup-*.txt

# --- Build/test artifacts purged from history 2026-07-11 (never re-track) ---
# The scratch build output dir: staged kernel, ELF/nm dumps, boot logs, etc.
# Regenerated every build; must never be committed.
/build/
# ESP staging: the bootable kernel + firmware nvram are build outputs.
# Keep esp/limine.conf and esp/EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI (config + bootloader);
# ignore the regenerated binaries.
esp/boot/kernel
esp/EFI/BOOT/kernel.bin
esp/NvVars
# All log files are transient (serial captures, boot/clippy/qemu runs).
*.log
# Clippy / build stdout+stderr capture dumps written to the repo root.
clippy_*.json
clippy_err.txt
clippy_out.txt
clippy_output.txt
clippy_sweep.txt
clippy_warning_counts.txt
build_check.txt
build_err.txt
build_out.txt
build_out2.txt
build_out3.txt
build_output.txt
boot_output.txt
full_build.txt
# Stray test/sweep output dumps and serial captures (transient build output).
sweep_test_out.txt
*_test_out.txt
serial_out.txt
serial_out*.txt

# Python bytecode caches left behind by the repo's own scripts (scripts/*.py).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Exception: this saved page is intentionally tracked (reference kept in-repo),
# even though the blanket *.html rule above ignores saved web pages.
!Aero Desktop (offline).html

# HarfBuzz sources fetched for reference by the Indic shaper work.
# Not ours, not built, not shipped.
.hbref/
# Operator's private instruction queue. Kept on disk, deliberately NOT tracked
# on the shared branches: it is a scratch inbox of raw notes to the agents, not
# a project document, and the operator asked for it to stay off GitHub
# (2026-08-14). `todo.txt` — the shared, agent-maintained one — IS still
# tracked; only `todo2.txt` is exempt.
#
# It IS versioned locally, just not here: the orphan branch `private/todo2`
# holds its history and is never pushed (./scripts/snapshot-todo2.sh appends to
# it; `git show private/todo2:todo2.txt` reads it back). It cannot live on a
# shared branch, because those are pushed constantly by three agents. This rule
# and the `pre-push` hook are two independent guards on the same thing: the
# rule stops it being staged by accident, the hook stops any push that carries
# it regardless of how it got committed. See scripts/hooks/pre-push.
/todo2.txt

# Synthetic oracle faces for the HarfBuzz sweep. Each is regenerated in one
# command from the tracked generator beside it — `gen_thai_legacy.py`,
# `gen_khmer_probe.py`, `gen_myanmar_probe.py` — and is a build artifact of that
# script, not a source file. Tracking them would put a few hundred KB of binary
# in history that no reader can diff and that any change to the generator
# immediately stales.
/gui/font/tools/thai-legacy/
/gui/font/tools/khmer-probe/
/gui/font/tools/myanmar-probe/
